 "At night, the lights are on. The fields are bright.": "80b9b48052",
 "By extending the daylight with electric lamps, farmers delay blooming and control when the chrysanthemums reach the market.": "33e034b86c",
 "Covering 341 hectares, the garden is Taiwan's largest center for growing and selling flowers, seedlings and bonsai.": "cb252708a7",
 "Farmers turn on the lights at night, so the chrysanthemums grow longer stems before they bloom.": "b234aa836a",
 "Gardeners shape the shrubs into birds and animals, an art called topiary that shows off Tianwei's horticultural skills.": "aa6432938a",
 "I ride my bike. I see a bird tree!": "e92c0f4be3",
 "Long ago, a young man went to China. He saw many flowers. He brought seeds home. Now Tianwei is a flower town!": "3da290e20e",
 "Look at the wall! It has a big painting.": "60274aefc1",
 "More than one hundred years ago, Wu Xiu-qi traveled to Zhangzhou and saw people growing flowers. He brought seeds and cuttings back to Tianwei and started a flower farm with his brother. In 1973, the area became the Highway Garden.": "005911acf3",
 "The road is flat and quiet, so it is easy to ride a bike and enjoy the flowers.": "ddd7ec47c9",
 "The village took its name from the settlers' ancestral home in Guangdong, and community art has since given it a new identity.": "7bf5617aca",
 "Tianwei Highway Garden is famous for its flower farms. Visitors can buy plants and seeds there.": "86ffd79105",
 "Tianwei has many flowers. They are beautiful!": "1747676726",
 "Tianwei's flower industry began over a century ago, when Wu Xiu-qi brought seeds and cuttings home from Zhangzhou. Plant trading and low-cost seedlings helped it spread, and in 1973 the government designated the area a horticultural zone. It was first called the Highway Park, but visitors kept looking for a park, so it was renamed the Highway Garden.": "377ac548b0",
 "Young people came back to their hometown and painted the old walls with bright colors.": "eb85882c37",
